    "_error_map_note": "Story 26.4 (dossier section 10, 774 codes parsed): keys are '<http_status>:<numeric body Code>' -- Microsoft returns application errors with generic HTTP 400/401/403 and the real classification key is the numeric Code inside ApiFaultDetail/AdApiFaultDetail Errors[] (body-first, HTTP fallback). Rate-limit codes are NOT in this map: 117 CallRateExceeded / 207 ConcurrentRequestOverLimit / 4204 Bulk throttling are declared in rate_limit_codes and raise core.quota.RateLimitError (breaker + re-queue) whatever the HTTP status. 400:2001-2101 is the ReportingService* validation family (columns 2015, aggregation 2007, dates 2009/2011/2041, scope 2019-2035, report id 2100/2101); 2100/2101 on a POLL of a previously valid reference are mapped by the connector to the canonical async 'expired' status (26.1 F-3) before this map applies. 5xx falls through to provider_transient via classify_http_error.",
    "rate_limit_codes": [
        "117",
        "207",
        "4204"
    ],
    "refetch": {
        "nightly_days": 3,
        "weekly_days": 30,
        "monthly_days": 90,
        "_note": "Dossier section 9: clicks ~2h, conversions ~3h, invalid-traffic adjustments up to a week+ (nightly 3d), conversions credited to the CLICK date with goal windows up to 90 days (weekly 30d, monthly 90d). Daily retention 36 months = hard backfill bound."
    },
